<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Syloson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Syloson was a brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polycrates">Polycrates</a>, tyrant of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samo">Samos</a>, who banished him. In exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, according to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a>, he gave his cloak to the young Darius, who as king repaid the gift by sending <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otanes">Otanes</a> to conquer Samos and install Syloson as tyrant around 517 BCE. His son Aeaces later ruled Samos as a Persian client.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/syloson.jpg" alt="Syloson" width="320" height="162" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ISLANDS_off_IONIA,_Samos._Circa_500-494_BC.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
